From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:39:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: google-flame: VBUS supply on the connector

Since b5817fa4026c ("arm64: dts: qcom: pm8150b: move vdd-vbus-supply to
connector nodes"), pm8150b.dtsi no longer gives the Type-C block its
VBUS supply: each board names it on its usb-c connector.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-google-flame.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-google-flame.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-google-flame.dts
index 2318a43af2e5..a2919efe98da 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-google-flame.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-google-flame.dts
@@ -1014,6 +1014,8 @@ connector {
 		power-role = "dual";
 		data-role = "dual";
 		self-powered;
+
+		vbus-supply = <&pm8150b_vbus>;
 		
 		source-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 900,
 		PDO_FIXED_SUSPEND |
